! MTF THF: modulation at one frequency (FRE) through the focus positions
! FFO/IFO/NFO.  Each position is the MTF with the image plane moved there; it
! equals a real THI SI move of the image followed by plain MTF (checked below
! on a singlet: the THF rows match the THI SI runs digit for digit).
RES osdtriplet
FFO -0.1
IFO 0.025
NFO 9
MTF THF ; GO
MTF THF ; SETFLD 3 ; FRE 100 ; GO
! singlet: THF vs a real image move
LEN NEW
EPD 20
YAN 0 5
INS S2
RDY S1 120
THI S1 5
GLA S1 NBK7
RDY S2 -50
THI S2 92.3
FFO -0.2
IFO 0.2
NFO 3
MTF THF ; SETFLD 2 ; FRE 50 ; NRD 32 ; GO
FFO 0
THI SI -0.2
MTF ; SETFLD 2 ; MFR 50 ; IFR 50 ; NRD 32 ; GO
THI SI 0.2
MTF ; SETFLD 2 ; MFR 50 ; IFR 50 ; NRD 32 ; GO
THI SI 0
! plain MTF honours FFO (same numbers as THI SI 0.2 above)
FFO 0.2
MTF ; SETFLD 2 ; MFR 50 ; IFR 50 ; NRD 32 ; GO
! one focus position; frequency beyond the cutoff
NFO 1
MTF THF ; FRE 600 ; NRD 32 ; GO
! bad input
MTF SIDEWAYS ; GO
MTF THF ; FRE 0 ; FRE ABC ; NRD 32 ; GO
MTF ; FRE 50 ; GO
